 "answer": "**I’d avoid outdoor exercise today and, if you can, stay indoors during periods of poor air quality.** Air-quality feeds for Kuala Lumpur are inconsistent, but some are reporting unhealthy readings for sensitive people, with higher levels forecast later. Since you have asthma, it’s sensible to be cautious; check Malaysia’s official APIMS reading for your nearest station before heading out. ([airindex.today](https://airindex.today/en/air-quality-index-kuala-lumpur-1735161?utm_source=openai))\n\nIf you do go out, keep it brief and easy. Keep your reliever inhaler with you and follow your asthma action plan. If you’re wheezing or getting short of breath and your reliever isn’t helping as your plan says it should, seek urgent medical care. ([cdc.gov](https://www.cdc.gov/heat-health/hcp/clinical-guidance/how-to-use-the-heatrisk-tool-and-air-quality-index.html?utm_source=openai))",
